---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, DISCLAIMER } from '../lib/site';

const title = 'Terms of Service – Globle Unlimited';
const description =
  'The terms governing your use of Globle Unlimited: acceptable use, intellectual property, disclaimers, limitation of liability, and governing law.';

const schema: Record<string, unknown>[] = [
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebPage', name: title, url: SITE.url + '/terms-of-service' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/terms-of-service" schema={schema}>
  <article class="prose legal">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › Terms of Service</p>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated mono">Last updated: {SITE.legalUpdated}</p>

    <p class="lede">
      These Terms of Service (&ldquo;Terms&rdquo;) govern your access to and use of
      {SITE.name} at {SITE.domain} (the &ldquo;Service&rdquo;). By using the Service, you agree to
      these Terms. Please read them carefully. If you do not agree, please do not use the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
    <p>
      By accessing or using the Service, you confirm that you can form a binding contract and that
      you accept these Terms and our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, which is
      incorporated here by reference. If you are using the Service on behalf of an organisation, you
      represent that you are authorised to accept these Terms on its behalf. These Terms apply to
      every visitor and user of the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be able to form a legally binding contract to use the Service. The Service is
      intended for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13. If you are a minor
      in your jurisdiction, you may use the Service only with the involvement of a parent or
      guardian. By using the Service, you represent that you meet these requirements and that your
      use complies with all laws that apply to you.
    </p>

    <h2>3. The Service</h2>
    <p>
      Globle Unlimited is a free, browser-based geography game. We may add, change, or remove
      features at any time. We may also limit, suspend, or discontinue the Service, in whole or in
      part, without notice. The Service is provided for personal, non-commercial entertainment and
      educational use. We do not guarantee that the Service will always be available or that it will
      be free of interruptions, delays, or errors.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Licence to use</h2>
    <p>
      Subject to these Terms, we grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable
      licence to access and use the Service for your own personal, non-commercial purposes. This
      licence does not allow you to resell, redistribute, frame, mirror, or commercially exploit the
      Service or its content. All rights not expressly granted to you are reserved by us.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <h3>Prohibited activities</h3>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the Service in any way that violates applicable law or regulation.</li>
      <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the Service, its servers, or related systems.</li>
      <li>Interfere with or disrupt the integrity or performance of the Service, including by
        scraping, overloading, or deploying automated tools beyond normal gameplay.</li>
      <li>Copy, modify, or create derivative works of the Service except as expressly permitted.</li>
      <li>Remove or obscure any proprietary notices, or misrepresent your affiliation with us.</li>
      <li>Use the Service to transmit malware or to engage in any fraudulent or harmful activity.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may investigate and take appropriate action against anyone who, in our sole discretion,
      violates this section, including blocking access to the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Service&rsquo;s design, code, text, graphics and original assets are owned by us or our
      licensors and are protected by intellectual-property laws. Map data is provided by
      <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Natural Earth</a>
      (public domain) and globe imagery is based on
      <a href="https://visibleearth.nasa.gov/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">NASA Visible Earth</a>
      (public domain); these are used in accordance with their terms. All other trademarks and
      brand names are the property of their respective owners.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Trademark and independence notice</h2>
    <p>
      {DISCLAIMER} This Service is an independent, fan-made project. Any references to the original
      game are nominative and do not imply any endorsement, sponsorship, or affiliation. If you are
      a rights holder and have a concern, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you send us ideas, suggestions, or feedback about the Service, you grant us a perpetual,
      irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free licence to use and incorporate that feedback for any
      purpose, without any obligation or compensation to you. We value your input and may use it to
      improve the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Accuracy of game content</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is for entertainment and educational purposes. While we strive for geographic
      accuracy using trusted open data, borders, place names, distances, and daily answers may
      contain errors or simplifications and should not be relied upon for navigation, legal,
      academic, or other authoritative purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Third-party links and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The Service may contain links to third-party websites and may display third-party advertising,
      including through Google AdSense. We do not control and are not responsible for third-party
      content, products, or practices. Your dealings with third parties, including advertisers, are
      solely between you and them. See our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for how
      advertising data is handled.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is provided on an &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo; basis,
      without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including warranties of
      merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, and non-infringement. We do not
      warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that geographic data and
      answers are free from inaccuracies. You use the Service at your own risk.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, we will not be liable for any indirect, incidental,
      special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of data, profits, or goodwill,
      arising from your use of or inability to use the Service. Our total liability for any claim
      relating to the Service will not exceed one hundred U.S. dollars (US$100). Some jurisdictions
      do not allow certain limitations, so some of the above may not apply to you.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Indemnification</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to indemnify and hold us harmless from any claims, damages, liabilities, and
      expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your misuse of the Service or your
      violation of these Terms or any applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Termination</h2>
    <p>
      We may suspend or terminate your access to the Service at any time, with or without cause or
      notice. You may stop using the Service at any time. Provisions that by their nature should
      survive termination (including intellectual property, disclaimers, limitation of liability,
      and indemnification) will survive.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Changes to these Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms from time to time. When we do, we will revise the &ldquo;Last
      updated&rdquo; date above. Your continued use of the Service after changes take effect
      constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms. We encourage you to review this page
      periodically.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of {SITE.jurisdiction},
      without regard to its conflict-of-laws principles. You agree to the exclusive jurisdiction of
      the courts located in {SITE.jurisdiction} for any dispute arising out of these Terms or the
      Service, to the extent permitted by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>17. General provisions</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Severability:</strong> if any provision of these Terms is held invalid, the remaining
      provisions will continue in full effect.
      <strong>Entire agreement:</strong> these Terms and the Privacy Policy are the entire agreement
      between you and us regarding the Service.
      <strong>No waiver:</strong> our failure to enforce any right or provision is not a waiver of
      that right.
      <strong>Assignment:</strong> you may not assign these Terms without our consent; we may assign
      them freely.
      <strong>Force majeure:</strong> we are not liable for delays or failures caused by events
      beyond our reasonable control.
    </p>

    <h2>18. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or visit our
      <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal { padding-block: var(--space-12); }
  .crumb { font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--text-mute); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .crumb a { color: var(--text-dim); }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h1); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .updated { color: var(--text-mute); font-size: var(--fs-small); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .legal ul { color: var(--text-dim); margin: var(--space-4) 0; padding-left: var(--space-6); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
